Package: poisselect
Type: Package
Title: Maximum Likelihood Estimation of Poisson Selection Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Sebastian", "Jung", email = "s_jung@stud.uni-bamberg.de",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Finn", "Metzler", email = "finn.metzler@stud.uni-bamberg.de",
           role = "aut"))
Description: Fits a Heckman-type selection model for count data by maximum
    likelihood. A Poisson outcome equation with log-normal unobserved
    heterogeneity is estimated jointly with a probit selection equation, so
    that the correlation between the two error terms corrects the bias that a
    plain Poisson generalised linear model incurs when the outcome is observed
    for a self-selected subsample only. The likelihood integral is approximated
    by Gauss-Hermite quadrature and evaluated entirely on the log scale. The
    fitted object has 'print', 'summary', 'plot', 'predict', 'coef', 'vcov' and
    'logLik' methods, and a simulator for the model is included.
